From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: soft reset the GPU before runtime suspend

The GPU's runtime suspend gates its clocks and marks it for hw_init, but
the oxili GDSCs only collapse once every device in the domain has
suspended, and the GPU's SMMU shares it with a 20 ms autosuspend. So a
GPU that suspends and resumes while the SMMU is busy comes back with no
power collapse and whatever state the last session left: hw_init then
reloads the microcode and sends CP_ME_INIT to a core that was never
reset, and the first job after it can hang. Pinning the SMMU on, so the
GDSCs never collapse, makes that happen several times a minute.

kgsl handles this in _adreno_start(): if either GPU regulator (the GX or
CX GDSC) is still enabled, it soft resets the core with RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD
before a3xx_start(). drm only does that in a3xx_recover().

Reset the core in pm_suspend instead, before the clocks go off, so it is
left the way a collapse would leave it whether or not the GDSCs actually
collapse. Doing it in hw_init would also work, but the reset clears the
RBBM power counter that devfreq takes its baseline from in
msm_gpu_pm_resume(), before hw_init runs, so busy time would go
backwards on every resume.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-12 09:44:39.069647193 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c	2026-10-12 10:03:55.058262597 +0400
@@ -375,6 +375,13 @@
 	return a3xx_me_init(gpu) ? 0 : -EINVAL;
 }
 
+static void a3xx_soft_reset(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
+{
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
+	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+}
+
 static void a3xx_recover(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	int i;
@@ -390,12 +397,23 @@
 	if (hang_debug)
 		a3xx_dump(gpu);
 
-	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
-	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
-	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+	a3xx_soft_reset(gpu);
 	adreno_recover(gpu);
 }
 
+static int a3xx_pm_suspend(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Runtime suspend only gates the clocks: the GDSCs collapse once the
+	 * SMMU, which shares them, has suspended too, and when it has not the
+	 * GPU comes back with its old state. Leave it reset, as a collapse
+	 * would. kgsl does the same when it finds the regulator left on.
+	 */
+	a3xx_soft_reset(gpu);
+
+	return msm_gpu_pm_suspend(gpu);
+}
+
 static void a3xx_destroy(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
@@ -579,7 +597,7 @@
 		.get_param = adreno_get_param,
 		.set_param = adreno_set_param,
 		.hw_init = a3xx_hw_init,
-		.pm_suspend = msm_gpu_pm_suspend,
+		.pm_suspend = a3xx_pm_suspend,
 		.pm_resume = msm_gpu_pm_resume,
 		.recover = a3xx_recover,
 		.submit = a3xx_submit,
